From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:04:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: give the guest the size of its window

The guest display kept the size given at start (1280x800 by default) and
the window scaled it, so a HiDPI window showed a blurry, enlarged
desktop. With CROSVM_GVM_FOLLOW_WINDOW the scanout follows the window:

- display_wl takes the size the compositor configures (any state) and the
  surface's exact scale from wp_fractional_scale_v1, keeps that logical
  size through the viewport whatever buffer the guest shows, and reports
  the window's pixel size once per change. With "fill" the toplevel asks
  to be maximized after its first acknowledged configure, so an embedding
  compositor (Casilda) gives it the widget's size.
- the GPU device offers that size as the preferred mode (display info and
  EDID) and raises the config interrupt; the guest's virtio-gpu driver
  re-reads both and sends a hotplug event, and GNOME moves to the new
  preferred mode.
- the EDID's physical size is chosen in whole centimetres so that GNOME's
  automatic scale (diagonal DPI over 135, or 110 from 20 inches up) is the
  window's scale: the guest desktop has the host's scale and the guest's
  logical size is the window's.
- a new guest resolution replaces the surface's buffers in place, so the
  window keeps its maximized state and focus and never shows an empty
  frame.
- pointer and touch map the window's logical extent onto the range the
  absolute input devices were created with, which stays fixed while the
  guest resolution changes.
- the base EDID timing's 16-bit clock wrapped for large modes (3392x2400
  at 120 Hz needs about 1160 MHz) and gave the guest a slow, wrong rate;
  it now carries the highest rate that fits, and the DisplayID timing the
  requested one (both preferred; the guest takes the higher rate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Purpose: Give the guest the size of its window.
Origin: https://github.com/yzddmr6/GunyahVM/commit/0aa0ad1dffc730909bbe71ce8520bfea3d34fad8
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
